  "body": "After preserving a Candidate, Runner now observes an acknowledged provider termination before releasing the attempt and performing receipt-bound cleanup. Cleanup no longer tries to mint a live lease permit after successful release. Failures during termination, required journal writes, release or cleanup return a typed `FINALIZATION_UNRESOLVED` error containing token-free preservation references and the original cause; they do not enter generic failure cleanup or issue a second release/requeue.\n\nRegression fixtures cover negative termination acknowledgements, termination errors, release committed with its response lost, cleanup refusal, cleanup completed with its response lost, and failed required/recovery journal writes. They assert actual retained or removed workspace artifacts, preservation references, queue/lease state and zero or one release. Existing test identities remain; six tests were added to the audited inventory.\n\nValidation: 110 Runner library tests pass; strict workspace/all-target Clippy and canonical inventory validation pass. The complete required lane on exact commit `bbcbea77de9bc8ab97822f62ebd3c17dc79c0297` passes: 1,221 standalone tests and 34 contract tests, plus lint, security, documentation and proof-custody checks. Independent source, fixture and inventory reviews accepted all 14 changed files.\n\nScope: this is component evidence. Native descendant observation, durable unknown-capacity retention beyond the existing lease TTL, atomic Candidate/Attempt/quota/verifier settlement, and end-to-end cleanup retry recovery remain open. The Operating HOLD remains in effect. Portal connected and packaged checks will be rerun with fresh accepted Runner/Gitd binaries after this change lands.\n",
